.TH LFS-POOL 1 2026-08-07 "Lustre" "Lustre User Utilities"
.SH NAME
lfs-pool \- commands used to manage OST pools and pool pinning via lustre.pin
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B lfs pool
.RB [ list | pin | unpin | pin_info ]
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ arguments ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B lfs pool
subcommands list OST pools, and manipulate the
.B lustre.pin
extended attribute of Lustre files and directories in order to record whether they are
pinned to a particular OST pool.  Pool pins are stored as YAML entries of the form
.B pool:
.IR POOL
inside the
.B lustre.pin
attribute, alongside any other keys that may be present.
.PP
The following subcommands are available:
.TP
.B lfs pool list \fR\fIFSNAME\fR[.\fIPOOLNAME\fR] | \fIPATHNAME\fR
List the pools on
.IR FSNAME ,
or the OSTs in
.IR FSNAME . POOLNAME ,
or the pool associated with
.IR PATHNAME .
This subcommand is also available as the top-level
.B lfs pool_list
command, kept for backward compatibility.
.TP
.B lfs pool pin
Ensure that a
.B pool
entry for the specified
.IR POOL
exists in the
.B lustre.pin
attribute of each target.
See
.BR lfs-pool-pin (1)
for full details.
.TP
.B lfs pool unpin
Remove the
.B pool
entry for
.IR POOL
from the
.B lustre.pin
attribute of each target.
See
.BR lfs-pool-unpin (1)
for full details.
.TP
.B lfs pool pin_info
Report whether the
.B lustre.pin
attribute of each target contains a
.B pool
entry for the requested
.IR POOL .
See
.BR lfs-pool-pin_info (1)
for full details.
.SH AVAILABILITY
The
.BR "lfs pool pin" ", " unpin " and " pin_info
subcommands are part of the
.BR lustre (7)
filesystem package since release 2.18.0.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR lfs (1),
